      "method": "Apply PiLp.contDiff_ofLp to g; use screenRatio_smooth for g_j/r; expand the two-by-two P and multiply by smooth q coordinates. Compact support follows support(screenAmplitudeOf) subset support(g).",
      "supplier": "SmoothScreenDualTensorR5.screenRatio_smooth"
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "target": "theorem axisCompact_uniform_null_gap (g : MomentumCoordinates → Fib) (hc : HasCompactSupport g) (ε : ℝ) (hε : 0 < ε) (hcut : ∀ y, ‖y.1‖ ≤ ε → g y = 0) : ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧ ∀ y ∈ tsupport g, δ ≤ shellNullFrequency y",
      "method": "If tsupport empty choose any delta. Otherwise support closure lies in norm(q)>=epsilon; shellNullFrequency_pos and continuity on compact support give a positive attained minimum. Optional explicit bound: if E<=M on support then u=r^2/(E+p)>=epsilon^2/(2*M).",
      "suppliers": [
