    {
      "id": "S4",
      "target": "theorem inverseNull_quasiMeasurePreserving : QuasiMeasurePreserving (fun z : Transverse × ℝ => nullMomentumCoordinates z.1 z.2) ((volume : Measure Transverse).prod (volume.restrict (Ioi 0))) (orbitalMeasure 0)",
      "method": "Prove the global nonnegative integral transport first for measurable functions, using withDensity, Tonelli, longitudinal_null_lintegral and inverseLongitudinal_null. It identifies the pushforward of dq*(du/u) with the existing orbital measure. On u>0, 1/u>0 so unweighted positive-u product measure is absolutely continuous relative to this weighted measure; obtain quasi-preservation. It transports arbitrary Lp a.e. representatives; do not assume a pointwise equality for the chosen Lp representative.",
